  "id": "random-noise",
  "term": "random noise",
  "definition": "Random noise is a moving visual pattern, created either by computer graphics or by conventional analog methods, that can be used to help people notice abnormalities in their visual field that they may not otherwise be aware of. In this context, it is a perceptual stimulus rather than a symptom or disorder.",
